---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GlassPanel from '../components/GlassPanel.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Child Safety"
  description="SoundCheck child safety standards, CSAE policy, and reporting."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-container px-5 py-12 md:px-8 md:py-16">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black text-chrome">Child safety standards</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl font-body text-silver">
        SoundCheck is committed to protecting children and preventing child sexual abuse and
        exploitation (CSAE). These standards apply to all users of our social concert platform.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <GlassPanel>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-chrome">Age requirement</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 font-body text-muted">
          You must be at least <strong class="text-chrome">13 years old</strong> to use SoundCheck,
          as stated in our <a href="/terms" class="text-cyan hover:underline">Terms of Service</a>.
          We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we learn that
          we have, we will delete that information promptly.
        </p>
      </GlassPanel>

      <GlassPanel>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-chrome">Prohibited content and conduct</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 font-body text-muted">
          SoundCheck strictly prohibits child sexual abuse material (CSAM), grooming, sexualization
          of minors, and any content or behavior that exploits children. Violations result in
          immediate account termination and reporting to appropriate authorities.
        </p>
      </GlassPanel>

      <GlassPanel>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-chrome">In-app reporting</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 font-body text-muted">
          Users can report concerning profiles, check-ins, photos, or messages directly in the app
          using the report option on any user-generated content. Our moderation team reviews reports
          and takes action within our enforcement guidelines.
        </p>
      </GlassPanel>

      <GlassPanel>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-chrome">Law enforcement and NCMEC</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 font-body text-muted">
          We comply with applicable laws regarding child safety. When we identify CSAM or credible
          threats to children, we report to the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children
          (NCMEC) and cooperate with law enforcement as required.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-muted">
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.missingkids.org/"
              class="text-cyan hover:underline"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">NCMEC (US)</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.inhope.org/"
              class="text-cyan hover:underline"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">INHOPE (international hotlines)</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </GlassPanel>

      <GlassPanel>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-chrome">Contact for child safety concerns</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 font-body text-muted">
          For urgent child safety reports or law enforcement inquiries, contact:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <a href="mailto:privacy@soundcheck.app" class="font-body text-cyan hover:underline"
            >privacy@soundcheck.app</a
          >
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-muted">
          Subject line: <strong class="text-silver">Child Safety Report</strong>
        </p>
      </GlassPanel>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
